Pixie: Did I get the spell wrong? I'm pretty sure-
Your eyes flutter open. Dappled sunlight streams down, mostly obscured by the massive trees overhead. In front of you is a small person, fluttering in midair on gossamer wings.
According to all known laws of aviation, there is no way that this person should be able to fly. Its wings are too small. And yet, somehow they do...
